  "name": "doi-10-5281-zenodo-3401424",
  "notes": "<p>Wind lidars allow new approaches to building and operating wind plants but also generate huge amounts of data. This white paper provides a short overview of how digitalization -- the process of converting information into discoverable, shareable, and actionable computer-readable data -- could help the wind energy industry benefit from wind lidar, and what needs to be done to make this vision a reality.</p>\n\n<p>We welcome feedback on the document. Please go to <a href=\"https://github.com/IEA-Wind-Task-32/white-paper-Task32-lidar-digitalisation\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">https://github.com/IEA-Wind-Task-32/white-paper-Task32-lidar-digitalisation</a> to find out how you can help improve this document.</p>",
